From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd939x-sdw: don't cache the interrupt clear
 registers

The interrupt clear registers are written by regmap-irq to acknowledge
each interrupt, so their cached value is the last acknowledgement. When
the TX device resumes, regcache_sync() writes that value back and clears
any interrupt raised while the device was suspended, before the alert
handler reads the status. A headset plugged in while the SoundWire link
is clock stopped is then never reported.

Mark them volatile, as wcd938x does.

Fixes: be2af391cea0 ("ASoC: codecs: Add WCD939x Soundwire devices driver")
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
@@ -1290,6 +1290,9 @@
 	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_STATUS_0:
 	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_STATUS_1:
 	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_STATUS_2:
+	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_CLEAR_0:
+	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_CLEAR_1:
+	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_CLEAR_2:
 	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_SWR_HM_TEST_0:
 	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_SWR_HM_TEST_1:
 	case WCD939X_DIGITAL_PIN_STATUS_0:
